   "stop_reason": "The paper's planned contrasts (exercise vs no exercise within mRNA-Seq and within Ribo-Seq) have n = 2 pooled replicates (3 mice each) per arm; the repository suitability check (tools/suitability.py:259 check_sample_size, MIN_GROUP=3) marks both planned comparisons not analyzable and decision_contract.py:172 rejects a valid design with that verdict. Scientifically the estimand is identified (edgeR on reconstructed counts, residual df = 2, exploratory label per the decision contract's small-n rule), so the block is a tool policy, not a data defect. Unblock: a runner/spec option to accept small-n planned two-group contrasts as exploratory (as run_joint_deseq2 'include' does, which still requires one analyzable planned comparison). Pooling assays or adding a pooled 4-vs-4 comparison only to pass the gate was rejected as not the paper's estimand."
  }
 ],
